# allow-verbs.baseline - the committed expectation for dashboard-server.py ALLOW_VERBS (the /act verb
# allow-list). verify-brain.ps1 regexes the literal out of the server source and diffs it against this file;
# ANY difference is a hard FAIL, because a new reachable verb is new attack surface.
#
# CHANGING THIS FILE IS THE APPROVAL STEP. It is only legitimate to edit it in the SAME commit as the
# dashboard-server.py change that adds or removes the verb. If verify-brain fails on this check and no such
# commit exists, the server source was modified out-of-band - treat it as tampering, not as a stale baseline.
#
# One verb per line, sorted. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored by the checker.
# captured 2026-08-18 from dashboard-server.py (14 verbs)
butler
date-night-refresh
encode-next
force-snapraid-sync
grab
qbit-pause
qbit-resume
refresh-recs
regen-now
reroll
restart-service
search-missing
tell-michael
upgrade4k
